# Milestone: M3
# Covers: REPL session persists var bindings across separate chunks (lines);
#         each REPL frame is its own chunk but shares the implicit Realm.
#
# defer-to: T20
#
# Reason: At M3, the REPL drives each line as a separate chunk with its own
# Namespace. Variables bound in one line are not visible in the next because
# each chunk gets a fresh Namespace (the parse-time binding scope).
# T20 (Strand C API) will add urbi_strand_set_realm to allow the REPL to reuse
# the same Realm across lines, preserving bindings.
#
# When T20 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the urbiscript source.
# Expected behaviour: line 1 binds x=41; line 2 reads x and computes x+1=42.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T20):
#   var x = 41
#   x + 1
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 41
#   [00000002] 42
